\subsubsection{Results of Pretrained Models}
Table \ref{tab:pretrain_1} and \ref{tab:pretrain_5} report \textit{Best@1} and \textit{Best@5} accuracy for different prompts. Overall, deepseek-R1 achieves the highest performance, and every model benefits from chain-of-thought prompts compared to zero-shot. However, we observe that some LLM-optimized codes actually degrade performance. This can happen for two reasons: First, the restructuring performed by the LLM can introduce new loop dependencies, increasing latency; Second, the pragmas inserted by LLMs may be less effective than the default optimizations inferred by the HLS compiler.
