We now introduce the notion of the \textbf{differential Shapley value}. For two data owners $A, B \in \mathbb{O}$, we define the differential Shapley value between $A$ and $B$ as $\Psi_\mathbb{O}(A, B)=\psi_\mathbb{O}(A)-\psi_\mathbb{O}(B)$.  We have the following useful result, a variation of Lemma 1 by~\citet{pmlr-v89-jia19a} on efficient data valuation.

