\subsection{Case GT100}%Dealing with the Overlapping of Cycles}
\label{sec:gt100} 
As previously discussed, the sum of the categories can exceed 100\% of cycles. This situation occurs because some hardware events partially overlap, and multiple stall causes are recorded in a single cycle. We resolve this excess of cycles by subtracting the exceeding fraction from some of the categories of the ISC stack so that it fits the 100\% of execution cycles. The question is from which categories should they be subtracted to fit 100\%.


