\subsection{Reciprocity and cycles}

Reciprocity and cycles are graph measurements which can be useful to indicate users' behaviors which represent central features for the circulation of a CC. 

In terms of graph edges, the \textit{reciprocity} $r_i \in \{0, \dots,N\}$ of the $i$-th node, $i \in \mathcal{N}$, is defined as
\begin{equation}
 r_i = \sum_{j \in \mathcal{N}} \delta_{ij} \delta_{ji},   
\end{equation}
\noindent thus providing the number of nodes that share with the $i$-th node transactions in both directions (not necessarily the same number). Figure~\ref{fig:recipDist} shows the distribution of reciprocity over the network. The maximum value of $r_i$ in 2022 is $564$ (out of the horizontal axis limit in Figure~\ref{fig:recipDist}), while in the other two years it is almost half, specifically $283$ in 2023 and $285$ in 2024. 

