\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Experimental details} 
\noindent{\bf Large Language Models:}
To verify the capability and biases of LLMs to predict ROP risk, we perform evaluations on a range of LLMs, including open-source general models, closed-source general models, and specialized medical language models.
For open-source general models, we use GLM-4 (9B)~\cite{glm2024chatglm}, Gemma-2 (27B)~\cite{riviere2024gemma}, Yi (34B)~\cite{young2024yi}, DeepSeek (V2-16B, R1-distill-llama-70B)~\cite{guo2025deepseek}, Mixtral-8*7B~\cite{jiang2024mixtral}, LLaMA-3.3 (70B)~\cite{llama3modelcard}, LLaMA-4~\cite{meta2025llama}, Qwen-3 (235B)~\cite{qwen3-2025} and Qwen-2.5 (0.5B to 72B)~\cite{qwen2.5}.
For closed-source general models, GPT-3.5~\cite{ouyang2022training}, GPT-4~\cite{achiam2023gpt}, GPT-4o~\cite{hurst2024gpt}, o3-mini, o4-mini, Doubao-pro~\cite{doubao2024pre}, ERNIE-3.5~\cite{ernie2024}, Baichuan-4~\cite{baichuan}, and Claude-3.5~\cite{claude2024} are used.
For specialized medical models, we use Medllama (7B), HuatuoGPT-o1 (7B) \cite{chen2024huatuogpt}, Doctorai (8B)\footnote{\url{https://ollama.com/}}, and Openbiollm (70B)~\cite{OpenBioLLMs}. 

