\noindent{\bf Performance of ICL Scheme:}
For the ICL scheme, the prediction accuracy of the LLMs for ROP risk also improves compared to the Instructional scheme.
For instance, the average performance improves by 15.48\% in the Claude-3.5.
However, although the ICL scheme improves model performance, it is not as effective as the CoT scheme. For example, in the Qwen-2.5, the average performance decreases by 7\%.
The reason for this is that, compared to the CoT scheme composed of known risk factors, the ICL scheme, made up of demonstration examples, more rigorously challenges the model's reasoning abilities and its intrinsic understanding of ROP disease.

\noindent{\bf Performance Comparison for Different Source Models:}
From another perspective, we evaluate the performance of different source models. 
In the Instructional scheme, the medical model Openbiollm achieves the best performance, with an ROP risk prediction accuracy of 47.73\%, which indicates that models fine-tuned with more specialized medical samples can achieve more precise ROP diagnostic capabilities.
For instance, the accuracy improves by 12.09\% compared to the LLaMA-3.3.
However, in the CoT and ICL schemes, the open-source Qwen-2.5 outperforms other LLMs.
The potential reason may be that Qwen-2.5 consistently outperforms other models in Chinese tasks, which aligns with the description by Qwen-2.5~\cite{qwen2.5}.
