\begin{theorem}
    Let $K,\phi$ be a filtered abstract $k$-complex, and let $f, g$ be two embedding functions of $K$ into $\R^d$. 
    Let $a_1, a_2, \cdots a_{n'}$ denote the discrete filtration values of $\phi$, without multiplicity, with $2 \leq n' \leq n $.
    Furthermore let $n = |V(K)|$, and let $\delta = \underset{v\in V(K)}{max} |f(v) -g(v)|_1 $.
    Let $K_a$ denote a triangulation of $\phi\inv (a)$ such that for every $a_i \leq a \leq a_{i+1}$, the family of $K_a$ are all different embeddings of the same abstract simplicial complex.
    Then 
    $$d_{\ReFLECT}((K,\phi, f),(K,\phi,g)) \leq 2\gamma_n \delta C_{k-1} \int_{a_{min}}^{a_{max}} C_{K_a}  da$$
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
We know from Theorem \ref{thm:ectstablity} that for each levelset $K_a$ (convex hull P),

$$d_{\ECT}\big{(}ECT(f(K_a)), ECT(g(K_a))\big{)} \leq 2 C_K C_d \sum_{p\in V(K_a)}\|f(p) - g(p)\|_2.$$
Since for most levelsets, none of the points $p$ will be vertices in $V(K)$ the right hand distance of the embedding functions is not the distance of $f,g$. 

Integrating over the parameter $a$ we obtain 

$$\int_{\R}d_{\ECT}\big{(}ECT(f(K_a)), ECT(g(K_a))\big{)} \  da \leq \int_{\R}2 C_{K_a} C_d \sum_{p\in V(K_a)}\|f(p) - g(p)\|_2 \ da.$$
The left side is, in fact our $\ReFLECT$ distance. We now obtain the stability in terms of the distance of $f,g$. 

\begin{align*}
d_\ReFLECT((K,\phi,f),(K,\phi,g) &\leq 2 C_d \int_{\R} C_{K_a}  \sum_{p\in V(K_a)}\|f(p) - g(p)\|_2 \ da \\ 
&\leq 2 C_d \int_{\R} C_{K_a}  \sum_{p\in V(K_a)}\|f(p) - g(p)\|_1 \ da \\
&\leq 2 C_d \int_{\R} C_{K_a}  \gamma_n \delta \ da \\
&\leq 2 C_d \gamma_n \delta \int_{\R} C_{K_a} \ da. \\
\end{align*}
With the restriction that each of the triangulations between critical homology values remain different embeddings of the same complex, this integral is simply an integer valued step function, and our upper bound is well defined. 
\end{proof}
