\subsubsection{Multi-fidelity MISC approximation}
The local timestepping error \mg{(LTE)} tolerance $\letol$ is used to define the \mg{different fidelities for the problem such that}
\begin{equation}\label{eq:models-parabolic}
    \miModel \mapsto \{\approxS{q}:\Gamma\to\R \text{ computed with LTE tolerance } \letol=10^{-\miModel}\}
\end{equation}
with associated model evaluation cost $\widehat{W}_{\miModel}=10^{\miModel/3}$ derived from \eqref{eq:parabolicwork}.
Symmetric Leja points and the two-step rule from \eqref{eq:rules} are used to form the MISC approximation.


