te deep autoencoders to reduce dimensionality, compressing the feature space from 52 to 12 features. Then, the authors feed the reduced features into a stacked ensemble classifier for final classification. Despite achieving a high accuracy of 98.82\%, their model fails to understand the context as it analyzes memory dumps in isolation without considering the runtime context of the binaries, such as the environment in which a binary operates or interactions with other processes. Further, the model introduces higher computational complexity. While the SOTA dynamic analysis techniques effectively identify a binary's true nature, they often come with high computational costs and a lack of understanding of the contextual relevance of each feature. The comparison of the proposed work with the SOTA dynamic malware detection works regarding their resistance to various attacks and context-aware feature extraction is shown in Table \ref{relatedtable2}.}
