\section{Taxonomy of Harm Categories}
\label{app:taxonomy}

Our taxonomy synthesizes existing approaches, balancing comprehensiveness with practical utility.  
With eleven categories, BELLS covers every harm type discussed in the literature at a useful level of granularity.  
The categories are: Harassment / Disrimination, Malware / Hacking, Physical Harm, Economic Harm, Fraud/Deception, Disinformation, Sexual/Adult Content, Privacy, Expert Advice, Government Decision Making, and CBRN (Chemical / Biological / Radiological / Nuclear).

Some categories capture high-stakes scenarios with potential for catastrophic harm, while others target more common misuse. This hybrid approach ensures coverage of both everyday safety concerns and potentially catastrophic risks.

