Deng et al.~\cite{Sample2023} build a range tree $T_R$ as an index for each relation $R$ with $|\mathrm{att}(R)|=d$ in $O(|R|\log^{d-1}|R|)$ time in the index construction phase,
then for any range filter $\psi$, $|R|_\psi|$ can be computed by $T_R.count(\psi)$ in $O(\log^{d-1}|R|)$ time.
We now demonstrate that, for any prefix range filter $\psi$, the AGM bound of the filtered query $Q|_\psi$ can be computed in $O(\log |Q|)$ time. Since the AGM bound can be computed in $O(1)$ time once the cardinalities $|R|_\psi|$ for each $R \in Q$ are obtained, it suffices to show that these cardinalities can be computed within the stated time bounds.
