For alignment quality assessment, we first get the token alignment on the test data using Eflomal and  we compare \psp and \sptgt using:

\paragraph{One-to-one ($\uparrow$).} Following \citet{hammerl-etal-2025-beyond}, this measures the proportion of source tokens that have exactly one aligned target token which is also aligned to exactly one token. We measure this on the source side due to its fixed tokenization.
%
% \gv{Not really clear. There can be only that many 1-1 links, if the text is well aligned but over tokenized, we would have a lower score if we measure it on the target side}

