\subsection{Machine Translation}

We evaluate our tokenizer on machine translation, hypothesizing that improved token correspondence between languages should simplify MT model training by making the task more similar to token-level translation rather than complex sequence-to-sequence mapping.

We use the same language pairs and tokenizers as in intrinsic evaluation, testing three vocabulary sizes with the largest available training set for each language pair. Our experimental setup uses \spsrc for input tokenization and \psp for output tokenization, with \sptrg replacing \psp as the baseline.

